    "formContent": "<div class=\"ielts-form-container\"><div class=\"form-section\"><div class=\"form-title\" style=\"text-align:center;font-weight:700;font-size:1.1em;margin-bottom:8px;\">Invasive species</div><p>Definition: an animal or plant that causes harm to an environment after being introduced by humans</p><p style=\"margin-top:6px;\">An invasive species can be a problem when it:</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; eats native species.</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; introduces a new <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"31\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> .</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; takes food from native species.</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; threatens an entire <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"32\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> .</p><p style=\"font-weight:700;margin-top:10px;\">How invasive species spread</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; accidentally e.g. via people returning from their <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"33\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> or on cargo ships</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; intentionally e.g. for pest control, or as <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"34\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> .</p><p style=\"font-weight:700;margin-top:10px;\">Examples of invasive species</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; Rhinella marina (toads)</p><p style=\"padding-left:42px;\">&ndash;&nbsp; were introduced to Australia from Hawaii in 1935 to eat a type of insect that was damaging the <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"35\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> plantations.</p><p style=\"padding-left:42px;\">&ndash;&nbsp; failed to solve the problem and became widespread in the north of Australia.</p><p style=\"padding-left:42px;\">&ndash;&nbsp; are poisonous for any species that eats them and reduce the food available for native frogs.</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; Japanese knotweed plants were popular among 19th-century gardeners in the UK.</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; Rhododendron plants prevent <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"36\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> from reaching native plants.</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; Grey squirrels from N. America reduce sources of food for the UK's native red squirrels and spread a <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"37\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> that kills red squirrels.</p><p style=\"font-weight:700;margin-top:10px;\">Tackling invasive species</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; Monitoring helps us to understand the <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"38\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> of invasive species and the impact they have.</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; Setting up a national <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"39\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> makes it easier to track them.</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; Asking the public to <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"40\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> and report them helps with monitoring.</p></div></div>",
